# Settings a build reads from its environment — copy the ones you need into
# .env.local (gitignored: never commit real values here). Vite reads both
# .env and .env.local; a variable set in the shell wins over either.

# The site's operator (CTA-182) — who the Privacy Policy and the Cookies Notice
# name as running the site; they fill %OPERATOR_NAME%, %OPERATOR_ADDRESS% and
# %PRIVACY_EMAIL% in src/views/blog/articles/app-pages/. Set all three of
# NAME, ADDRESS and PRIVACY_EMAIL, or none: with none the build has no legal
# pages (no /privacy, /cookies, footer links or sitemap lines). Any of them can
# have a value per language, <VARIABLE>_<LANG> for any language the app has —
# the _HE lines below are the Hebrew pages' own; a new language adds its own
# lines the same way (SITE_OPERATOR_NAME_FR=). Unset, a language shows the
# plain value. The build warns of a SITE_* variable it reads none of (a typo,
# a language the app has not got). The deploys read the repository's variables
# of the same names, every SITE_* one (docs/in-app-pages.md §5).
SITE_OPERATOR_NAME=
SITE_OPERATOR_NAME_HE=
SITE_OPERATOR_ADDRESS=
SITE_OPERATOR_ADDRESS_HE=
SITE_PRIVACY_EMAIL=
